<https://w3id.org/def/cleets/data#activity/turnover-2026-11-24> a prov:Activity ;
    rdfs:label "Fleet turnover path from observed scrappage and second-hand entry"@en ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Companion notebook to \"Predicting electric vehicle adoption in Wales from open data integrated in semantic knowledge graphs\" (manuscript, 2026): EVAdoptionWalesPredictionsModels24Nov.ipynb, Sections 6 and 11 of the companion notebook; paper Sections 4.6 and 5.6 to 5.8; Supplementary Tables S15 to S18. Values taken from: turnover_district_inputs_and_results.csv, turnover_path_central_district_quarter.csv, turnover_path_2045_by_scrappage_period.csv, weibull_ceiling_on_cars.csv."@en ;
    dcterms:source "notebook exports: turnover_district_inputs_and_results.csv, turnover_path_central_district_quarter.csv, turnover_path_2045_by_scrappage_period.csv, weibull_ceiling_on_cars.csv" ;
    rdfs:comment "A stock-flow model of private cars by district, fuel and year of first registration, started from the cars licensed at 2026 Q2 (VEH9901). Cars leave at the retention rates observed for British cohorts between year ends (VEH1111; 2021 to 2025 in the central scenario) and are replaced one for one, so each district's private car stock is held at its 2026 Q2 level. Cars enter private keepership at the ages at which they do so in each district, new and second hand, and their battery-electric share follows the sales rule for new cars (24.7% in 2026 rising to 80% in 2030 and 100% in 2035), adjusted for the lower uptake of Welsh private keepers, which converges on the national mix by 2030. The result is a path, an estimate of what the sales rule delivers to the private car stock, and not an upper bound. The Weibull ceiling (14-year median life, every scrapped car replaced by a new one) is kept as a benchmark."@en ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-11-24"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:used <https://w3id.org/def/cleets/data#dataset/VEH0105>,
        <https://w3id.org/def/cleets/data#dataset/VEH0142>,
        <https://w3id.org/def/cleets/data#dataset/VEH1111>,
        <https://w3id.org/def/cleets/data#dataset/VEH9901> ;
    cleets:notebookStage "Sections 6 and 11 of the companion notebook" ;
    cleets:paperSection "Sections 4.6 and 5.6 to 5.8; Supplementary Tables S15 to S18" .

